      "content": "Explain that meritocracy assumes a level playing field, but systemic racism ensures unequal starting lines through historical exclusion. For instance, if one neighborhood was historically denied bank loans, generations of resulting lower property values create a persistent barrier to generational wealth accumulation, regardless of an individual's work ethic. This demonstrates that systemic barriers pre-determine outcomes, making \"pulling yourself up\" insufficient when the ladder itself is unequally placed.",
